{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1415859-x-rays-and-seeing-through-solid-objects","id":1415859,"title":"X-rays and seeing through solid objects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-28T11:21:02-07:00","id":1415859,"title":"X-rays and seeing through solid objects","content":"Hi.<br /> <br /> Probably the most basic question ever asked here...what spheres would you need to see through solid objects?<br /> <br /> Im asking this because Forces 1 states you can see x-rays, which, to my understanding, is not the same as <b>you can see as if the x-rays were being shot from your eyes. </b><br /> <br /> I guess it would involve some level of Matter. Not sure. Sphere system is awesome, but sometimes messy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T11:33:34-07:00","id":1415860,"title":"","content":"I'd say Forces 1 and Matter 1 would let you see through walls easily by viewing the light through them, while Correspondence 1 and Forces 1 would let you see the light in an entire area. With how the magick works, your character could easily believe they have x-ray vision and just have the ability to understand what they see based off what spheres they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26088-actual_table","name":"Actual_Table","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26088_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T13:32:28-07:00","id":1415879,"title":"","content":"Matter 1 lets you see specific matter patterns, so if you wanted to see through a solid object, I'd recommend Forces 1 and Matter 1. Correspondence 1 lets you see around things in a small area near you, so combining it with either Forces 1 or Matter 1 would let you see through solid objects.<br /> <br /> Basic way spheres work:<br /> <br /> Rank 1. Detect sphere and very limited manipulation (minor effects to enhance skills, channel Quintessence with Prime)<br /> Rank 2. Minor control. About 150 lbs weight telekinesis with Forces, suggestions with Mind, minor probability alterations with Entropy, etc.<br /> Rank 3. Minor bring forth or negate target sphere subject. Forces lets you change one type of energy to another, negate it or create it (creation requires Prime) and with Life you can greatly alter yourself and hurt others. Correspondence 3, well you can teleport and you can see several places at once. Matter 3 lets you make some complex things, but not the craziest things.<br /> Rank 4. Significant control. Move an automobile with Forces telekinesis, turn enemy into a natural animal, create magic items with Prime, open a Hermes portal with Correspondence.<br /> Rank 5. Massive power. The real limits here are successes and what's just plain not allowed in Mage. You can literally make lifeforms, create pocket dimensions, blow up city blocks with forces and make minds.<br /> <br /> <i>Enlightened Grimoire</i> is a good source for what you can do. It compiles many magickal effects. Unlike M20 How Do You Do That?, Enlightened Grimoire is not trying to rewrite all the Mage rules on casting. Instead, being a compilation, you get a lot of summary on magical effects and references to the Mage books they appeared in if you want more. For example, if you were interested in enhanced senses, you'd check out that section of Enlightened Grimoire and get some ideas. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T15:13:44-07:00","id":1415892,"title":"","content":"Man, I had no idea that book existed! Thank you so much!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}